# GetFreeBit.com — Cursor rules

## Stack
- Next.js App Router (TypeScript), Tailwind CSS, SEO-first programmatic pages.
- Brand, ads, affiliates, and disclosure copy live in `src/site.config.ts`.
- Dataset / SEO templates live in `src/data/dataset.json`.
- Content strategy & voice: `.cursor/rules/getfreebit-engine.mdc` (always apply).

## Brand
- Site: **GetFreeBit** · Domain: `https://www.getfreebit.com`
- Niche: free crypto earnings, yield, Web3 onboarding (four pillars in the engine rule).
- Never hardcode brand name, colors, domain, or affiliate URLs in components — use `siteConfig`.

## Non-negotiables
- Never edit build-engine / programmatic page logic unless explicitly asked:
  - `src/app/guides/[slug]/page.tsx`
  - `src/app/w/[word]/page.tsx`
  - `src/lib/dataset.ts`
  - `scripts/lib/word-html.mjs`, `scripts/lib/word-seo.mjs`
- Monetized UI must surface `siteConfig.affiliateDisclosure`.
- No get-rich-quick copy, unverified token claims, or undisclosed tracking links.

## SEO / schema.org
- Use existing helpers (`SEOHead`, `HeadMetadata`, dataset graph builders).
- Supported: **SoftwareApplication**, **FAQPage**, **HowTo** (Calculator when the niche needs it).
- Do not invent JSON-LD shapes that break `scripts/assert-faq-schema.mjs` or `scripts/assert-seo-titles.mjs`.

## Dataset workflow
- Do not hand-write huge `dataset.json` payloads in chat.
- Generate with `scripts/generate_dataset.py`, overwrite `src/data/dataset.json`.
- Slugs, `primaryKeyword`, tags, and FAQs must map to a GetFreeBit pillar.

## Deployment
- Prefer Cloudflare Pages (GitHub connected).
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL` must match `siteConfig.domain`.

## Editing hygiene
- Change only files required for the request.
- Match existing chrome, ads slots, guides, and SEO patterns.
